57.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481104/college-football-trolls-week-11","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Watch best moments and top plays live from Week 11","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50474063/week-11-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Darian Mensah dices up ex-team Duke as Miami rebounds from first loss","description":"Miami quarterback Darian Mensah diced up his former team Saturday, finishing with 382 yards and a touchdown in the 36-25 victory over Duke.","published":"2026-11-14T23:57:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50484151/darian-mensah-dices-ex-team-duke-miami-rebounds-first-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest strengthens CFP case with 'statement' win at SMU","description":"No. 13 Wake Forest made a statement to the College Football Playoff selection committee with a 49-7 blowout of SMU on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-15T00:41:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483729/wake-forest-strengthens-cfp-case-statement-win-smu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Vols lose top receiver Matthews to knee injury vs. Texas A&M","description":"Tennessee leading receiver Mike Matthews suffered a right knee injury in the second quarter of Saturday's game at Texas A&M.","published":"2026-11-14T23:16:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50483677/vols-lose-top-receiver-matthews-knee-injury-vs-texas-am","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia commit, DL Marcellus Young Casario died after 'sudden medical emergency'","description":"Marcellus Young Casario, a Georgia football commit, died Friday after experiencing a \"sudden medical emergency,\" according to his high school.","published":"2026-11-14T20:36:58.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482223/georgia-football-commit-marcellus-young-casario-dies-suddenly","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma AD rips Ole Miss, SEC; Rebels defend travel effort","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny ripped the SEC and Ole Miss for the \"inexplicable\" decision to move its game to Sunday, while the Rebels defended their travel efforts.","published":"2026-11-14T23:54:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482206/oklahoma-ad-infuriated-sec-ole-miss-sunday-game","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Clemson QB Reynolds to have MRI on knee; backup Vizzina (ankle) also hurt","description":"Clemson quarterback Tait Reynolds is having an MRI on his injured knee, and backup Christopher Vizzina was sent to the hospital to evaluate his ankle.","published":"2026-11-14T23:52:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50482105/clemson-qb-tait-reynolds-suffers-leg-injury-slide","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Central Oklahoma AD trolls Ole Miss amid FAA crisis-forced kickoff change","description":"The Division II school offered Ole Miss fans attending its Oklahoma matchup free admission due to the kickoff date change.","published":"2026-11-14T22:28:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481529/central-oklahoma-troll-ole-miss-faa-decsion","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ohio State WR Smith sets Big Ten record, states Heisman case","description":"Ohio State wide receiver Jeremiah Smith broke yet another record, eclipsing the Big Ten mark for career receiving yards while also making his Heisman Trophy case in Saturday's win over Northwestern.","published":"2026-11-14T23:15:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50481134/ohio-state-jeremiah-smith-sets-big-ten-receiving-record","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5067875/zach-lutmer","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Lutmer"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Zach Lutmer","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Lutmer","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:24Z","intro":"Zach Lutmer (born November 5, 2004) is an American college football defensive back for the Iowa Hawkeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lutmer attended Central Lyon High School in Rock Rapids, Iowa, where he played defensive back and quarterback. During his career he set school records for total yards, rushing yards and points scored. As a sophomore, Lutmer was the Class 2A Player of the Year after recording 1,194 passing yards, eight passing touchdowns, 1,609 rushing yards with 23 rushing touchdowns on offense and four interceptions, with two returned for a touchdown on defense. As a junior, he had 1,016 passing yards with eight touchdowns, 1,246 rushing yards with 22 touchdowns, and four interceptions with one returned for a touchdown. During his senior year he had 1,357 passing yards with 16 touchdowns, 1,562 rushing yards with 22 touchdowns and three interceptions. Lutmer committed to the University of Iowa to play college football."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Lutmer played in two games and redshirted his first year at Iowa in 2023. As a redshirt freshman in 2024, he played in all 13 games and had 14 tackles and one interception. Lutmer entered his redshirt sophomore year in 2025 as a starter."}]}}